# Whoships

> {{ t.oneLiner }} It reads GitHub's API with the user's own sign-in, directly from the Mac: read-only, no server in between, no account with the developer. Sample data is always free; watching your own organization is free for {{ site.trialDays }} days, then a one-time purchase of €{{ site.price.eur }} / US${{ site.price.usd }} (no subscription). Requires macOS {{ site.minMacOS }} or later. Current version: {{ site.version }}.

Key facts:
- Watches one GitHub organization on github.com (including GitHub Enterprise Cloud). GitHub Enterprise Server is not supported yet. Mac only; not on iPhone, iPad, Windows or Linux.
- Ten watchers: {% for w in watchers %}{{ w.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Refresh every 3 minutes (your own PRs), 15 minutes (organization activity) or 60 minutes (delivery, security, CI health).
- Shows in desktop widgets (small to extra large), the menu bar, a full-desktop dashboard behind windows, and macOS notifications.
- Explains why CI failed (tests, lint, build, timeout, out of disk, out of memory, network, access denied and more) from the check, the failed step and the job log.
- DORA metrics from GitHub Deployments, releases or merges to production branches; a deploy counts as failed when a hotfix or revert lands within 24 hours.
- Sign in with GitHub (OAuth device flow) or a classic personal access token with repo, read:org and read:user scopes. Organizations that restrict OAuth apps need an owner to approve Whoships once.
- Privacy: GitHub data and the sign-in stay on the Mac. The App Store version sends nothing to the developer; the whoships.app version sends anonymous usage statistics (no GitHub data), which can be turned off.
- Available as a direct download from whoships.app (license key, sold via Paddle); Mac App Store version coming soon.
- Not affiliated with GitHub, Inc.
- Website and app available in: {% for l in site.locales %}{{ l.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.

